1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,199
Under a sky thinning of smoke,

2
00:00:03,239 --> 00:00:07,913
Soraya Tahir stood in the middle
of Azadi Square and sang.

3
00:00:07,953 --> 00:00:12,693
Not a war song — an old Persian
song for the end of winter,

4
00:00:12,733 --> 00:00:17,960
for flowers opening, one the
revolution had never managed to ban.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,778
Women without hijabs, old
men with faded flags,

6
00:00:21,818 --> 00:00:25,595
parents holding children
joined in, one by one.

7
00:00:25,635 --> 00:00:29,695
The Basij came out onto
Vali-e Asr Avenue that day.

8
00:00:29,735 --> 00:00:32,347
But they didn't move to crush it.

9
00:00:32,387 --> 00:00:37,330
One of them set his baton down
on the pavement and sang along.

10
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:40,706
Someone laid a spring flower on top of it.

11
00:00:40,746 --> 00:00:46,493
Two days later, that image would be
shared more than any other on earth.

12
00:00:46,533 --> 00:00:48,743
The war had broken the city.

13
00:00:48,783 --> 00:00:53,123
But spring didn't stop —
spring is older than the war.
